# {{ .Name }}: a service built on gox

gox (`github.com/guilhermebr/gox`) is probably newer than your training data.
Look its API up with the commands below instead of guessing.

## Rules that always hold

- `main()` is `gox.MustNew(...)`, the `Register` calls, then `a.Run()`. gox owns
  start order, config, logging, health, metrics and shutdown: do not rebuild them.
- Handlers are plain `net/http` with Go 1.22 patterns:
  `a.HandleFunc("GET /invoices/{id}", h.get)`, `r.PathValue("id")`. `"GET /{$}"`
  is the exact root; `"GET /"` matches every path.
- Fail with gox errors and render them: `gox.Error(w, r, gox.NotFound("invoice %s", id))`.
  Never `http.Error` or hand-written error JSON.{{ if .Web }} HTML handlers use `web.Error`.{{ end }}
  A gox error's message and details reach the client; keep internals in the cause
  with `gox.WrapError(err, code, "public message")`. Any other error renders as a
  500 "internal error" and is logged.
- Config is fields on `Config` in `cmd/{{ .Name }}/main.go` (it embeds
  `gox.BaseConfig`) with `conf` tags, read from `{{ .Prefix }}_*` variables. Secrets carry
  `mask`. `help:` text has no commas (a comma cuts it short). Add every variable
  to `.env.example`; nothing loads a `.env` file.
- Handlers get dependencies through `Register(a, deps...)`, so tests pass `nil` or
  fakes. Every handler gets a test like `internal/hello/handler_test.go`.
- A response is buffered until its handler returns; one still running at
  `{{ .Prefix }}_HTTP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT` becomes a 504. SSE, WebSockets and streamed
  responses do not work.
- An accessor panic (`a.HTTPClient()`, `<module>.From(a)`) names the option missing
  from `gox.New`: add that option.
- Never: a router, ORM or DI framework; `os.Getenv`; a goroutine that outlives the
  request outside `gox.Component` or `gox.Periodic`; mutating the shared HTTP
  client; importing `github.com/guilhermebr/gox/pkg/...` except `pkg/storage`,
  `pkg/mail`, `pkg/i18n`, `pkg/middleware` and `pkg/httpclient`; datastore settings
  in `BaseConfig`.

## Layout

- `cmd/{{ .Name }}/main.go`: `Config`, `gox.MustNew(options...)`, the `Register` calls, `a.Run()`.
- `internal/<feature>/`: `handler.go` with `Register(a *gox.App, deps...)`, tests beside
  it. `internal/hello` is the example: copy its shape, then replace it.
{{- if .Postgres }}
- `migrations/`: `NNNNNN_name.up.sql` and `.down.sql`, embedded, run at boot.
{{- end }}
{{- if .Web }}
- `internal/<feature>/views/`: templ components; `*_templ.go` is generated from `*.templ`.
- `web/layout/`: the page shell and the error page. `static/`: embedded `css/` and `js/`.
{{- end }}
- `.env.example`: the `{{ .Prefix }}_*` variables to set; `--help` lists every one.

## Look it up (matches the versions in go.mod)

- API: `go doc github.com/guilhermebr/gox` lists the root package, `go doc gox.Periodic`
  shows one symbol, `go doc github.com/guilhermebr/gox/<module>` a module in go.mod.
- Variables: `go run ./cmd/{{ .Name }} --help` prints every `{{ .Prefix }}_*` variable with
  its type and default.
- Recipes, task-sized and build-checked, live in the gox module directory:
  `go list -m -f '{{ "{{.Dir}}" }}' github.com/guilhermebr/gox` (empty output: run
  `go mod download github.com/guilhermebr/gox` first). Read `docs/recipes/README.md`
  there, then only the recipe you need. Recipes keep code in one `main.go` for
  brevity; here it goes in `internal/<feature>` behind `Register`.
- `llm.txt` in that directory exports everything as one file for tools without a
  shell; do not read it whole.

## Read first for your task

- A JSON endpoint: `internal/hello`, then recipes `add-http-route` and `write-handler-test`.
- Background or scheduled work (jobs, cron, queues, workers, retries):
  `.claude/skills/gox-background-work/SKILL.md`.
- A capability not in go.mod yet (auth, OpenAPI, email, file storage, payments,
  webhooks, analytics, Temporal, Supabase, outbound API calls
{{- if not .Postgres }}, a Postgres database{{ end }}
{{- if not .Web }}, HTML pages{{ end }}):
  `.claude/skills/gox-add-feature/SKILL.md`.
{{- if .Postgres }}
- Tables, queries, transactions, migrations, database tests:
  `.claude/skills/gox-postgres/SKILL.md`.
{{- end }}
{{- if .Web }}
- Pages, forms, htmx partials, layout, static assets: `.claude/skills/gox-web-ui/SKILL.md`.
{{- end }}
- Anything else (health checks, pagination, rate limits, CORS, problem+json, i18n,
  SPA): the recipe index.

## Done

- `make test lint` passes. Lint is golangci-lint v2.11.4, the version CI pins
  (`go install github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@v2.11.4`);
  `make fmt` fixes formatting findings.
- `go mod tidy` after importing a module for the first time.
{{- if .Web }}
- After editing a `.templ` file run `make generate` (templ is pinned in the Makefile);
  never edit `*_templ.go` and never install templ. `make assets` once vendors htmx and
  Alpine.js into `static/js`.
{{- end }}
